<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gopalarajavamshavali</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gopalarajavamshavali is a chronicle of the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, written partly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> and partly in Nepal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhasa">Bhasa</a> and compiled in the late 14th century, probably under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayasthiti-malla">Jayasthiti Malla</a>. It lists the dynasties of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a> from the legendary cowherd kings and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kirata">Kiratas</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licchavi">Licchavis</a> and Mallas, with more detailed records for later reigns. It is the oldest surviving chronicle of Nepal.</p></div>
